.TH GIT-TREE 1 2026-11-04 "git-tree 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-tree \- commit graph of every branch, with an interactive browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git tree
.RI [ "git log options" ]
.RI [ revision ...]
.RB [[ \-\- ]
.IR path ...]
.br
.B git tree
.BR \-h " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git tree
draws the history of every local branch, remote branch and tag, one row per
commit. Every line of history keeps its own column and colour: a branch-off is
drawn on its fork point's row and a merge on the merge commit's row, so lines
stay in their column instead of drifting between rows. The checked-out branch
runs straight down the left edge. Refs are shown as labels; a local branch
whose remote counterpart is on the same commit is shown once, marked
.BR \[u21C5] .
Author, date and abbreviated hash sit in aligned columns on the right.
.PP
In a terminal,
.B git tree
opens an interactive browser. Enter on a commit shows its full message with
the files it changed below; Enter on a file shows its diff. Merges are shown
against their first parent. When standard output is not a terminal the graph
is printed as plain text.
.PP
All arguments are passed to
.BR git\-log (1),
so limits such as
.BR \-n ,
.BR \-\-since ,
.B \-\-author
and paths apply.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR Up / Down ", " j / k
Move the selection, or scroll a diff.
.TP
.BR PgUp / PgDn ", " b / Space
Move a page.
.TP
.BR Home / End ", " g / G
Go to the first or last item.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected commit, or the selected file's diff.
.TP
.BR J / K
Scroll a commit message that is longer than its half of the screen.
.TP
.B /
Search the commits, files or diff lines. Matches are highlighted and the
selection jumps to the next one as you type. The search is a literal, smart-case
match: case-insensitive unless the query contains a capital letter.
.B Enter
keeps the search,
.B Esc
or Backspace on an empty query cancels it and returns to where it started.
.TP
.BR n / N
Go to the next or previous match, wrapping around the ends.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the current search, otherwise go back one level. In the graph it quits.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of usage and keys. Run as
.BR "git tree \-\-help" ,
git shows this page instead.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, otherwise the status of the failing
.B git
command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-log (1)
